target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestCheckRefusesAnUnreadableRecord'
expect: consulted gh for a run whose record did not decode
why:    the ORDER is load-bearing, not tidy. Fingerprint reads Cycles, which is SHORT by one row for every cycle row that failed to decode, so a report gate run before the derivations is checking numbers no honest report could ever match — and it is checking them against a record the run has already been told is unreadable. The derivations refuse such a run; nothing upstream of them does.
--- old
	conv, err := r.Convergence()--- new
	if !ReportLanded(runID, r, repo) {
		_ = runID
	}
	conv, err := r.Convergence()